      "reason": "Option content. The PCNA technical data sheet prints 3,153 lb as \"Curb weight\" with no qualifier, while the PCNA and Porsche AG press releases say that figure is the lightest configuration with the optional Weissach Package and magnesium wheels. Porsche does not state the weight of the standard car in any source opened; Kelley Blue Book's saving of about 38 lb implies roughly 3,191 lb.",
      "resolution": "Used 3,153 lb, Porsche's own curb weight, under weight step 3 (an optioned car's curb weight: Weissach Package and magnesium wheels), since Porsche publishes no standard-car figure. A standard car is about 38 lb heavier."
    },
